    "updated_at": "2025-01-27T18:39:26Z",
    "body": "@davidkna \n\n>Ok. But if you want, you could make another PR that adds C++ file extensions to the C module or adds conditional styling options if C++ files are detected.\n\n\nSo should I abandon the work on my PR https://github.com/starship/starship/pull/6528 ?\n\nThe reason I want to include this is primarily to have different symbols for c and c++ projects and don't face the timeout issues with custom module in `starship.toml`\n\nI sometimes have projects that have both `c` and `cpp` files having different symbols representing that I am in such an env is very nice.\n\nkind of like this,\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d8dcb40f-b01c-49d1-8dff-0e064c7b1a98)\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8238d960-828a-4896-add3-46da7d649c9c)\n\nwant to know the exact direction you want us to take for this module? since it seems too many ppl have asked for this module and implemented in exactly the same way as I did and have never gotten around to merging the module. \n\nAsking because I would like to work on something that would actually be allowed in the project and achieve what I want.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
